-- title:
--   Descent between publications is transitive
-- statement:
--   For every payload type `V`, cluster `W` and keys `(t₁, v₁)`, `(t₂, v₂)`, `(t₃, v₃)`: if `Descends W t₁ v₁ t₂ v₂` and `Descends W t₂ v₂ t₃ v₃` then `Descends W t₁ v₁ t₃ v₃`. Nothing is assumed about `W`: `Descends` is the reflexive-transitive closure of `Parent`, where `Parent W t v t' v'` says that a publication of key `(t', v')` was sent with ghost parent `(t, v)`.
